{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOn 2026-10-18 the production MCP tickets clone (`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`) forked from `origin/tickets`, and every MCP gate refused with `stale-store` for about 50 minutes. The 2026-10-18 comments establish 3 causes:\n- During a blue-green deploy, the retiring container's detached compaction sweep held the shared clone's write lock.\n- Nothing pushed the fork until a client wrote.\n- Push contention logs below the default WARNING level, so the host showed nothing.\n\nThe 2026-11-03 comments add 1 reporting gap: 23 untracked pre-compaction event files appear in fsck as `snapshot_inconsistent` / `orphan_event`. This ticket carries the 2026-11-03 operator decisions.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **SIGTERM stops the sweep at a ticket boundary.**\n   - Why the sweep misses SIGTERM: it runs in a detached worker (`compact_trigger.run_sweep`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:152`) started with `start_new_session=True` (`src/rebar/_proc.py:121`). The MCP server is PID 1 (`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh:346` `exec \"$@\"`), and `docker stop` (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:456`) signals only PID 1.\n   - Worker side: `run_sweep` installs a SIGTERM handler that only sets a stop flag. Before the next ticket, `_sweep_should_yield` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:296`) checks the flag, logs at WARNING, and ends the loop. The fold in progress commits, and the end-of-run push still runs. A fold that raises still rolls back via `_abort_fold` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:384`, called at :500/:503).\n   - Server side: the MCP SIGTERM handler (`make_sigterm_handler`, `src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:66`) closes intake as today. Then a new `compact_trigger.stop_local_sweep(tracker)` reads the worker-lock stamp (`_acquire_trigger_lock`, :105). It signals the pid only when `lock_owner._describe_stamped_pid` (`src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py:181`) reports it live in this PID namespace, so it never signals another container's worker.\n   - Before exit: the handler waits, within the existing grace, for that worker to exit and the store write lock to be free, then sets `should_exit`. The shared clone stays.\n2. **Idle-timer sync.**\n   - A daemon thread started beside `start_startup_store_sweep` (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:294`; `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:569`) runs a new `sync.idle_sync(tracker)` every 120 s.\n   - It stops when the gauge is draining, and holds the gauge during each run.\n   - `idle_sync` calls `reconverge` (`src/rebar/_store/sync.py:224`, which fetches and merges but never pushes), then calls `push.push_after_commit` when HEAD is ahead of the remote or a push-pending marker exists.\n   - The interval is a module constant: no new config key, env var, or lock.\n3. **Default-level logging.**\n   - The gap: the default level is WARNING (`src/rebar/_logging.py:91`), but push contention logs at DEBUG (`src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:163`), and a busy lock silently skips reconverge (`sync.py:263`).\n   - `idle_sync` logs at WARNING when a run ends PUSH_PENDING (with its reason, such as non-fast-forward), DIVERGED, or lock-skipped (naming the holder), and once when a pending marker clears.\n   - A run that is already current logs at DEBUG. `_terminal_severity` is unchanged, so CLI writes stay quiet.\n4. **fsck row kind.**\n   - `dirty_tracker_classes` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py:282`) gains `untracked_events`: untracked `*.json` files that are not `.tmp-event-*`, SNAPSHOT, or `.retired`.\n   - They are reported as `TRACKER_DIRTY_UNTRACKED_EVENT`, report-only like `TRACKER_DIRTY_TMP_EVENT` (`_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS`, :258), because an append in progress briefly owns such a file. The detail says whether a tracked `.retired` copy exists.\n   - `_active_event_map` (`src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py:343`) skips them, so `_check_snapshot` (:366) no longer also emits `snapshot_inconsistent` / `orphan_event` for them.\n   - `doctor.py` `_DIRTY_FINDING_SPECS` (:152) gets a report-only entry; doctor never moves these files.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe work lands as 3 independent Gerrit changes: (1), (2+3), and (4).\n\nFiles: `src/rebar/_commands/{compact_trigger,compact,fsck_tracker_health,fsck_scan,fsck,doctor}.py`, `src/rebar/{_mcp_serving,_mcp_health,mcp_server}.py`, `src/rebar/_store/sync.py`, `src/rebar/schemas/fsck.schema.json`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/concurrency.md`, plus the new tests named below.\n\nOut of scope:\n- The stale-cache refusal. It did not reproduce, and the freshness path has no TTL cache.\n- `env_id_mismatch`, done in `7ea86184dac`.\n- Production cleanup. `rebar store maintenance --clean` (`src/rebar/_commands/tracker_maintenance.py:193-249`) repairs only stranded index entries and foreign top-level paths. It has no rule for untracked event or `.tmp-event-*` files in ticket dirs, and no runbook runs it against the server clone. A separate ticket, linked `discovered_from`, tracks the cleanup.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo autouse fixtures, and no new `tests/_*.py` helpers. Each child process is bounded by a timeout and reaped in `finally`.\n- **Sweep:** a bounded child runs the real `_run_sweep` with a stubbed fold that logs start and end lines. It gets SIGTERM during ticket 2 and must exit 0 after \"end 2\", with no \"start 3\". In a second test, a bounded child holds the stamped worker lock and exits after `stop_local_sweep`. A forged other-namespace stamp is not signalled.\n- **MCP handler:** using fakes, check that retirement runs before `should_exit` is set.\n- **Idle sync:** use a temp store with a bare remote and 1 unpushed commit, with the loop at a short interval. The remote must receive the commit, and a WARNING \"delivered\" record must be logged. When the remote rejects the push, a WARNING naming PUSH_PENDING must be logged (caplog at WARNING).\n- **fsck:** an untracked event file with a tracked `.retired` copy must produce exactly 1 `tracker_dirty_untracked_event` row (`counted: false`), with no `snapshot_inconsistent` / `orphan_event` for it. A tracked active source must still report `snapshot_inconsistent`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1–AC4 of the 2026-10-18 plan are recorded as met or moot. AC1/AC2 were met by the 2026-10-18 host-evidence comments: the fork point, 9 local-only commits, and the blue-green overlap as the writer. AC3/AC4 were moot because the clone converged at 03:41 UTC without repair.\n- [ ] On SIGTERM, a detached sweep finishes its in-flight fold and exits before the next ticket: `pytest tests/unit/test_compact_sweep_sigterm.py` passes.\n- [ ] The MCP SIGTERM handler signals only a sweep worker that is live in its own PID namespace, and sets `should_exit` only after that worker exits and the write lock is free, within the grace: `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_retire_sweep.py` passes.\n- [ ] The MCP server's 120 s `idle_sync` timer delivers an unpushed commit with no client write, and logs undelivered, diverged, lock-skipped, and recovered outcomes at WARNING: `pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_idle_sync.py` passes.\n- [ ] `rebar store fsck --output json` reports untracked event files as `tracker_dirty_untracked_event` (`counted: false`), not as `snapshot_inconsistent` / `orphan_event`: `pytest tests/unit/test_fsck_untracked_event.py` passes.\n- [ ] With the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exit 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes before each push, and each change merges with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After merge, the host's `mcp-deployed-sha` equals or descends from the last merged SHA (read-only SSM check).","title":"Retiring MCP container's compaction sweep and silent push failures let the server tickets clone fork"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793738068032487001,"uuid":"d89ab117-f51c-462a-a08d-c7503067a793"}